claim.claim-text:
receiving (1905) a first signal from a first sensor (305);
determining (1910) a first projection sequence to display in response to the first signal from the first sensor (305);
determining (1915) a first translucent display (105) and a corresponding first projector (125) to display the first projection sequence;
transmitting (1920) instructions to the first projector (125) to project the first projection sequence onto the first translucent display (105);
receiving (1925) a second signal from a second sensor (305);
determining (1930) a second projection sequence to display in response to the second signal from the second sensor (305);
determining (1935) a second translucent display (105) and a corresponding second projector (125) to display the second projection sequence; and
transmitting (1940) instructions to the second projector (125) to project the second projection sequence onto the second translucent display (105).

receiving a third signal from a third sensor (305);
determining a third projection sequence to display in response to the third signal from the third sensor (305);
determining a third translucent display (105) and a corresponding third projector (125) to display the third projection sequence; and
transmitting instructions to the third projector (125) to project the third projection sequence onto the third translucent display (105).

receiving a fourth signal from a fourth sensor (305);
determining a fourth projection sequence to display in response to the fourth signal from the fourth sensor (305); and
transmitting instructions to the third projector (125) to project the fourth projection sequence on the third translucent display (105).

a first translucent display (105);
a second translucent display (105);
a first sensor (305);
a second sensor (305);
a first projector (125) corresponding to the first translucent display and configured to project a first projection sequence onto the first translucent display (105);
a second projector (125) corresponding to the second translucent display configured to project a second projection sequence onto the second translucent display (105); and
a projector controller (135) in communication with the first sensor (305), the second sensor (305), the first projector (125), and the second projector (125),
wherein the projector controller (135) is programmed to:

receive (1905) a first signal from the first sensor (305);
determine (1910) the first projection sequence to display in response to the first signal from the first sensor (305);
determine (1915) the first translucent display (105) and the corresponding first projector (125) to display the first projection sequence;
transmit (1920) instructions to the first projector (125) to project the first projection sequence onto the first translucent display (105);
receive (1925) a second signal from the second sensor (305);
determine (1930) the second projection sequence to display in response to the second signal from the second sensor (305);
determine (1935) the second translucent display (105) and the corresponding second projector (125) to display the second projection sequence; and
transmit (1940) instructions to the second projector (125) to project the second projection sequence onto the second translucent display (105).
